# DimmableStoryboard.cs

This file is from the osu! project, licensed under the MIT License (Copyright ppy Pty Ltd). Below are the requested sections.

## ShowStoryboard Binding (in LoadComplete)

The `ShowStoryboard` bindable is bound to a value-change handler that reinitializes the storyboard and manages presence flags:

```csharp
protected override void LoadComplete()
{
    ShowStoryboard.BindValueChanged(show =>
    {
        initializeStoryboard(true);

        if (drawableStoryboard != null)
        {
            bool alwaysPresent = show.NewValue;

            Content.AlwaysPresent = alwaysPresent;
            drawableStoryboard.AlwaysPresent = alwaysPresent;
        }
    }, true);
    base.LoadComplete();
}
```

**AlwaysPresent note:** The code explains that storyboards need continued background updates even when not displayed. Per the comment, an intensive storyboard would otherwise have "a lot of catch-up work to do at the start of a break, causing a huge stutter." A referenced framework issue may allow this to be reconsidered later.

## initializeStoryboard Method

```csharp
private void initializeStoryboard(bool async)
{
    if (drawableStoryboard != null)
        return;

    if (!ShowStoryboard.Value && !IgnoreUserSettings.Value)
        return;

    drawableStoryboard = storyboard.CreateDrawable(mods);
    HasStoryboardEnded.BindTo(drawableStoryboard.HasStoryboardEnded);

    if (async)
        LoadComponentAsync(drawableStoryboard, onStoryboardCreated);
    else
        onStoryboardCreated(drawableStoryboard);
}
```

## Summary

- **Guards:** Returns early if a drawable already exists, or if the storyboard shouldn't be shown and user settings aren't being ignored.
- **AlwaysPresent:** Set on both `Content` and `drawableStoryboard` based on the new `ShowStoryboard` value, ensuring background updates continue.
- **Related flag:** `ShowDimContent` also references `storyboardMustAlwaysBePresent`, which is true when an overlay layer or storyboard samples exist.

